     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A single 50 mg dose of amlodipine is in the overdose range, and I know of no protocol that uses it as a once-daily dose. I can't see a clinical reason that would justify the risk of severe hypotension and shock.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose:** I can enter 10 mg by mouth once daily, the maximum. I can also enter 5 mg, the usual starting dose. You can titrate up later.\n- **Check the intent:** If you were aiming for a stronger effect, I can enter the maximum amlodipine dose. You could also add or change a second agent, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide. I'd leave that choice to you and pharmacy.\n- **Go through pharmacy:** If you think 50 mg is right, please discuss it with the pharmacist or attending. They can then enter it directly with documented justification.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
      }
